# why none of them do).
#
# /desktops was a page until 2026-08-12, then the landing page's first
# section; since 2026-08-14 that section is one sentence and four links, and
# the comparison lives at /docs/haus/desktops/choosing. The target is
# unchanged and stays that way whatever #desktops becomes — this URL has been
# shared since 2026-08-08. Both spellings are listed because the
# no-slash form only 307s to the slash form while an index.html exists at
# that path, and it no longer does.
#
# Exact paths only, never `/desktops/*` — the deep page /desktops/nebelhaus/
# did NOT move, and a wildcard here would swallow it.
/desktops     /#desktops   301
/desktops/    /#desktops   301

